issue=f'''<!-- R2 ISSUE START --><article id="trackcivil-raildata" class="card build-notice"><p class="eyebrow">3R.2 · REAL RAIL DATA / TOPOLOGY / PROCUREMENT · 19 OCTOBER 2026</p><h2>The linked rail CAD does not match its section drawing.</h2><p>The supplier’s linked30ASCE paper section3040 has79.375mm height and base width. The linkedIGES imports with <strong>88.9 ×88.9mm</strong> face-envelope and304.8mm segment length:9.525mm, or12%, larger in height/base. SourceCMunits and importerMMunits were checked; both face-only and complete-shape extents agree. This is not a rolling tolerance adjustment.</p><p>The40-root/40-face, zero-solid surface model is kernel-valid, but that does not establish component identity. It is <strong>excluded from the project’s accepted geometry</strong>. No alternative rail family is asserted and it is not scaled, renamed or put into a rotatable train model as30ASCE. Exact source hashes, units, locators and an editable read-only inspection script are retained.</p><p>Joint data also differ: Kimes narrative5/8×2¾inbolt; its table/drawing5/8×3in; Harmer’s historical set5/8×2½in, with a different bar length. These are not interchangeable assemblies merely because all mention30ASCE. Supplier-confirmed mating faces, hole/grip/thread and joint details are required before ordering or drilling.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/rail-data-disposition.json">CAD / joint disposition</a><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/inputs-and-sources.json">Exact data / dates / source hashes</a><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/inspect-source-cad.py">Editable read-only CAD audit</a></div></article>
<article id="trackcivil-raildemand" class="card"><h2>Bounded rail-support demand—not a rail or tie-spacing approval</h2><p>The paper30ASCE reference gives I=4.10in⁴ and head/base section moduli2.55/2.70in³. These are nominal geometry, not a rail axle-load rating. The coach upper allocations13,200kg regular and11,000kg accessible, divided equally over8wheels, give16.181/13.484kN static wheel probes. Actual wheel imbalance and the unselected locomotive axle arrangement may govern.</p><p>Source computes18ideal cases:2coach allocations ×3unaccepted load factors ×3unaccepted spans. At the0.6m span probe below, a centered point load acts on an ideal simply supported bay. M=Pℓ/4; σ=M/Z; δ=Pℓ³/(48EI), with assumed E=200GPa. <strong>Paper section properties are used—not the mismatchedIGES.</strong></p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Coach</th><th>Unaccepted load factor</th><th>Static wheel kN before factor</th><th>Nominal head bending MPa</th><th>Ideal deflection mm</th></tr></thead><tbody>{supportrows}</tbody></table></div><p>No adequacy or safety factor is claimed. Actual support sharing/voids, multiple wheels, joints, lateral/contact/thermal/buckling/fatigue loads, material condition and allowable strength remain absent. P/2 ideal reactions are not governing tie/ballast loads for every wheel position. No tie spacing is selected from this simple model.</p><p>Nominal30lb/yd class corresponds to{quantity['single_rail_kg_per_m']:.4f}kg/m per rail, or{quantity['two_rails_kg_per_track_m']:.4f}kg per metre of single track. This is a material reference, not an actual order or certified lifting weight; route lengths, cuts/turnouts and spare allowances remain null.</p><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/calculations.json">18support cases / formulas / SI conversions</a></article>
<article id="trackcivil-topology" class="card"><h2>Routing recommendation remains conditional on real terrain</h2><p><strong>Study lead:</strong> a continuous one-direction loop, keeping the locomotive leading in normal guest service through both origin andNorthPole stops. This is a technical operating preference, not a final property route. Survey and accepted curves, stations, drainage and access must establish feasibility.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Topology</th><th>Normal movement</th><th>Condition before selection</th><th>Interfaces to engineer</th></tr></thead><tbody>{toporows}</tbody></table></div><p>Off-station evacuation cannot depend solely on recovery to a station. Fire, blocked route or traction/brake failure can prevent movement. Retain independent rescue access and qualified procedures. Later second-train use requires accepted route occupancy, separation and fault-response design; no timetable or collision-protection performance is assumed.</p><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/topology-and-operating-decision.json">Topology / reversing / recovery decision record</a></article>
<article id="trackcivil-procurement" class="card"><h2>Twelve coordinated technical procurement packages</h2><p>This schedule is prepared for design development. Nothing has been sent, ordered or purchased; project stock, lead time, configured part numbers and quantities remain unconfirmed. Real supplier links are evidence leads, not a qualified shopping list. Preserve farm-crew fabrication/installation where released, with specialists responsible for the rail processes, interfaces and acceptance they own.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Accountable discipline</th><th>Exact technical return before release</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pkgrows}</tbody></table></div><p>Sequence: technical-data/interface closure → released coordinated prototype and proof section → measured/tested interface freeze → first complete track/train/stations → separately engineered future second-train provisions. No delivery dates, durations, quantities or financial projections are invented.</p><h3>Current primary evidence</h3><ol>{src}</ol><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/technical-procurement-schedule.json">Editable technical procurement schedule</a><a class="button" href="assets/track-r2/build_issue.py">Editable calculations / issue source</a></div><p>3R.2 completes this bounded component/topology/procurement review, not3R or a fabricated track. No new project CAD or fabrication drawing is claimed. Next3S.1 consolidates the actual configuration/drawing/interface/release register and accountable outstanding evidence, then continues supportable fabrication/installation/commissioning/operations development.</p></article><!-- R2 ISSUE END -->'''
